{"type":"text","timestamp":1794322487730,"sessionID":"ses_e3a0f5faeffeaja4roFLLuM44w","part":{"id":"prt_1c5f45994001gzyYzDum4Icd8U","messageID":"msg_1c5f4493e001G54jvXaVITbVfg","sessionID":"ses_e3a0f5faeffeaja4roFLLuM44w","type":"text","text":"<think>Concurrency is handled correctly (6 × 3 = 18 ≤ 20; the 7th would exceed).\n\nNow let's clean up the test data dirs and move to the frontend. I'll remove the data-test dirs later.\n\nNow the frontend. Let me set up Tailwind CSS v4.\n\nSteps:\n1. `cd frontend && npm install -D tailwindcss @tailwindcss/vite` — check network access to npm registry works.\n2. Update vite.config.ts to include the tailwindcss plugin.\n3. Create src/index.css with `@import \"tailwindcss\";`\n4. Import it in main.tsx.\n5. Write components.\n\nLet me first check that npm install works in the sandbox (network through a read-only cache).</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794322487700,"end":1794322487726}}}
