{"type":"text","timestamp":1794322611245,"sessionID":"ses_e3a0f5faeffeaja4roFLLuM44w","part":{"id":"prt_1c5f63c1e001MzW7Htx6H8Ynqh","messageID":"msg_1c5f62e4f001jPle8tQ6uXvvZT","sessionID":"ses_e3a0f5faeffeaja4roFLLuM44w","type":"text","text":"<think>Note: `verbatimModuleSyntax: true` requires type-only imports to use `import type`. I used `import { useState } from \"react\"` (value import, fine) and `React.FormEvent` (a type used as a namespace reference — with verbatimModuleSyntax, `React.FormEvent` requires React to be in scope as a value import). Let me change AuthPanel to `import type { FormEvent } from \"react\"` and use `FormEvent`.\n\nAlso in vite.config.ts, `import react from \"@vitejs/plugin-react\"` is a value import — fine. But vite.config.ts is included in the tsconfig with `types: [\"vite/client\"]` — vite.config.ts needs node types for `defineConfig`? No, it doesn't.\n\nHmm, `allowImportingTsExtensions` requires noEmit — we have noEmit: true. OK.\n\nLet me now write the remaining components: DayPicker/AvailabilityPanel, BookingForm, ReservationsPanel, AdminPanel, and App.\n\nAlso fix the FormEvent import in AuthPanel.</think>\n\n","time":{"start":1794322611230,"end":1794322611242}}}
